-- title:
--   Gauss ring of K meets K₀ in O₀ (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing an element $\zeta$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Inside the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ consider two intermediate fields over $L$: first $K$, assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the quotients $\iota(p_f)/\iota(p_g)$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms $f, g$ of equal weight for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where $H$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$); and second $K_0$, assumed equal to the same base change applied to [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 M')`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), with $K_0 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ whose members are exactly those $f$ for which there exist $x, y \in A[[T]]$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f \cdot \iota_L(y) = \iota_L(x)$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, where $\iota_L$ denotes coefficientwise passage along $A \to L$ followed by the inclusion of power series into Laurent series; let $O_0$ be a valuation subring of $K_0$ characterised by the same condition on the underlying Laurent series. Then, giving $K$ the $K_0$-algebra structure coming from the inclusion $K_0 \le K$, an element $x \in K_0$ has its image in $W_0$ if and only if $x \in O_0$.
--
--   This is the statement that the Gauss (Igusa-type) valuation ring $W_0$ attached to $A$-integral $q$-expansions on the level-$q^2M'$ modular function field lies over the corresponding Gauss ring $O_0$ of the $\Gamma_0(M')$ floor, in the case $q = 2$, so that $O_0$ is exactly the contraction of $W_0$ along $K_0 \hookrightarrow K$. It feeds the analysis of the $\infty$-branch of the covering, being used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLocalHom_and_isSeparable_residueField_of_eq_comap_gauss_of_levelH_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLocalHom_and_isSeparable_residueField_of_eq_comap_gauss_of_levelH_of_eq_two).
